{
  "title": "Is it? Are you? Questions with be",
  "kind": "grammar",
  "cefr": "A0",
  "estMinutes": 8,
  "intro": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Form: questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "To make a question, put am / is / are BEFORE the person or thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "header": true,
      "rows": [
        [
          "positive",
          "question"
        ],
        [
          "You are a student.",
          "Are you a student?"
        ],
        [
          "It is a cat.",
          "Is it a cat?"
        ],
        [
          "I am late.",
          "Am I late?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Short answers"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "header": true,
      "rows": [
        [
          "question",
          "yes",
          "no"
        ],
        [
          "Are you …?",
          "Yes, I am.",
          "No, I'm not."
        ],
        [
          "Is it …?",
          "Yes, it is.",
          "No, it isn't."
        ],
        [
          "Am I …?",
          "Yes, you are.",
          "No, you aren't."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "title": "Short answers",
      "points": [
        "Answer with the same verb: Are you …? → Yes, I am.",
        "In positive short answers, do not use the short form: Yes, I am. (not Yes, I'm.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. Questions with question words"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "en": "Where are you from?",
      "note": "question word + be + person"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "en": "How old are you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "en": "What is it? / What's it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Be careful!"
    },
    {
      "type": "mistake",
      "wrong": "You are a student?",
      "right": "Are you a student?",
      "why": "Put are first."
    },
    {
      "type": "mistake",
      "wrong": "Yes, I'm.",
      "right": "Yes, I am."
    },
    {
      "type": "mistake",
      "wrong": "Where you are from?",
      "right": "Where are you from?"
    }
  ],
